## 9. Python Code Block

```python
def greet(name):
    print(f"Hello, {name}!")
    return True

greet("World")
```

## 10. JavaScript Code Block

```javascript
function greet(name) {
    console.log(`Hello, ${name}!`);
}
greet("World");
```

## 11. Plain Code Block

```
This is a code block.
Without any coloring.
```

## 12. HTML Code Block with Preview

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; padding: 20px; }
        .card {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7c3aed, #ec4899);
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="card">
        <h1>Live Preview!</h1>
        <p>This HTML renders live.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

## 13. Code Block with Line Highlights

```python {title="app.py" linenos hl=[3,7]}
import asyncio
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class User:
    name: str
    email: str

async def fetch_users():
    await asyncio.sleep(1)
    return [User("Ali", "ali@example.com")]
```

